// A MODULE-QUALIFIED free-function call carries the callee's parameter type
// into a literal argument, so an out-of-range one is refused AT THE LITERAL
// (DF-238a, FIXED).
//
// The literal used to stay at platform `Int`: an out-of-range one was SILENTLY
// TRUNCATED rather than refused (`qualcall.take_byte(300)` compiled and the
// callee received 44), and on a 32-bit target one wider than the platform word
// fell out of the fold domain as an internal compiler error. Every other
// spelling of the same call was correct — the bare selective import, the bare
// glob import, a qualified STATIC METHOD and a qualified CONSTRUCTOR all
// range-checked the literal — so the hole was the qualified free-function path
// alone, which resolved the callee and then checked the arguments against its
// RAW declared types.
//
// The two CONTROLS in `main` are the qualified member paths that were always
// correct; they are here so a fix cannot pass by breaking them.
//
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: integer literal 300 does not fit in `UInt8`
// COMPILE-FLAGS: --module-path qualcall={TESTDIR}/modules/qualcall238a
import qualcall

func main() {
    // The two CONTROLS first: both of these are refused today, and must stay
    // refused by whatever fixes the line below.
    let ok = qualcall.Byte238a.of(255)
    print(ok.value)

    // The finding.
    print(qualcall.take_byte(300))
}
